<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry Douglas Warden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1800">1800</a>–<a href="/years/1856">1856</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry Douglas Warden was a British army officer who served as British Resident in the territory between the Orange and Vaal rivers. In 1846 he founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bloemfontein">Bloemfontein</a> as his headquarters, and from 1848 he administered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-river">Orange River</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">Sovereignty</a> with few troops and little money. His boundary lines between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> farms and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sotho-people">Basotho</a> lands caused conflict, and after his defeat at Viervoet in 1851 he was removed from office.</p></div>
